ment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-24T04:35:09Z","email":"agent@replit.com","name":"Replit Agent"},"message":"Add office project management manual gap audit report\n\nReplit-Commit-Author: Agent","tree":{"sha":"8496b77cdae819fb31bee34a1563f10d8a44e6a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/safe-lanes/TechnicalMoudle/git/trees/8496b77cdae819fb31bee34a1563f10d8a44e6a2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/safe-lanes/TechnicalMoudle/git/commits/14a200ff3a459483ff92a919e2ad59f3b32123ed","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/207944715?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/replit-agent/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/replit-agent/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/replit-agent/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/replit-agent/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/replit-agent","id":207944715,"login":"replit-agent","node_id":"U_kgDODGT8Cw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/replit-agent/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/replit-agent/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/replit-agent/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/replit-agent/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/replit-agent/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/replit-agent","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/safe-lanes/TechnicalMoudle/commit/14a200ff3a459483ff92a919e2ad59f3b32123ed","node_id":"C_kwDOP13NqNoAKDE0YTIwMGZmM2E0NTk0ODNmZjkyYTkxOWUyYWQ1OWYzYjMyMTIzZWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/safe-lanes/TechnicalMoudle/commit/cf658d19a7c83b9b664c5210b6fca577b9069efe","sha":"cf658d19a7c83b9b664c5210b6fca577b9069efe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/safe-lanes/TechnicalMoudle/commits/cf658d19a7c83b9b664c5210b6fca577b9069efe"}],"sha":"14a200ff3a459483ff92a919e2ad59f3b32123ed","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/safe-lanes/TechnicalMoudle/commits/14a200ff3a459483ff92a919e2ad59f3b32123ed"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/224569240?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/safe-lanes/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/safe-lanes/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/safe-lanes/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/safe-lanes/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/safe-lanes","id":224569240,"login":"safe-lanes","node_id":"U_kgDODWKnmA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/safe-lanes/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/safe-lanes/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/safe-lanes/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/safe-lanes/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/safe-lanes/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/safe-lanes","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/safe-lanes/TechnicalMoudle/commits/7d519173051b24a7a0e938ae8723b6ea8f155eb7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T15:45:20Z","email":"support@sl-sail.com","name":"support"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T15:45:20Z","email":"support@sl-sail.com","name":"support"},"message":"assistant: multi-tenant Data API authentication — tenant from the module-signed identity + service secret (pilot-verified in MT mode, NOT deployed)\n\nGap: in multi-tenant mode the central assistant''s call to POST /assistant/execute carries no SAILERP\nBearer (the browser''s JWT never leaves the browser<->module hop), so tenantMiddleware refused it with\n401 and no tenant database could be selected.\n\nFix (inside the existing MT Phase-2 design, no exemption, no browser header trusted): tenantMiddleware\nconsults assistant-api/serviceTenant.ts for /assistant/manifest|execute. execute''s tenant is the\nidentity token''s tenantDomain - a value THIS module copied from the JWT-verified domain when it minted\nthe token under tenantMiddleware - accepted only with the shared service secret; both are verified\n(HMAC + timing-safe compare). A token without tenantDomain is refused (401 invalid_identity, fail\nclosed). manifest is static tool metadata: service secret only. Every other /technical/api route keeps\nthe Bearer rule unchanged; single-tenant mode is byte-identical (middleware inert).\n\nVerified on the pilot shore switched to multi-tenant mode (master pms_master_pilot: tenant ''pilot'' ->\npms_arch, tenant ''pilot-b'' -> pms_arch_b lazily migrated on first access, SHIP-WKFV mapped with its\nkey; ship sync still drains to zero). scripts/verify-assistant-multitenant-auth.ts (TRACKED harness,\n21 checks) PASSED: mint refuses no/expired/foreign-secret/no-domain/unknown-domain JWTs; execute refuses\nno/wrong secret, missing/tampered/expired identity, identity without tenant; tenant A -> its database\n(overdue 142); tenant B identity asking A''s vessel -> unknown in B; Ship-type user refused; ship\ncontainer 403 shore-only for manifest/execute/mint. Real widget with a SAILERP-shaped HS256 session\n(tenant A) -> 142 through the central assistant.\n\nStill pending (mock identity is not production identity trust): genuine SAILERP login; whether the\nproduction JWT carries domain/userType as this test''s JWT does; role/user id remain browser-forwarded\nx-user-* headers (same trust as the module''s RBAC guards). Documented in docs/ASSISTANT-API.md 3.1.\ntsc 294.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4685efa74e80253eae6266b37a378d6c0fa42ef9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/safe-lanes/TechnicalMoudle/git/trees/4685efa74e80253eae6266b37a378d6c0fa42ef9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/safe-lanes/TechnicalMoudle/git/commits/7d519173051b24a7a0e938ae8723b6ea8f155eb7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/224569240?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/safe-lanes/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/safe-lanes/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/safe-lanes/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/safe-lanes/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/safe-lanes","id":224569240,"login":"safe-lanes","node_id":"U_kgDODWKnmA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/safe-lanes/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/safe-lanes/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/safe-lanes/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/safe-lanes/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/safe-lanes/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/safe-lanes","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/safe-lanes/TechnicalMoudle/commit/7d519173051b24a7a0e938ae8723b6ea8f155eb7","node_id":"C_kwDOP13NqNoAKDdkNTE5MTczMDUxYjI0YTdhMGU5MzhhZTg3MjNiNmVhOGYxNTVlYjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/safe-lanes/TechnicalMoudle/commit/049305dff1911342a06d4f7fa631463b88acc840","sha":"049305dff1911342a06d4f7fa631463b88acc840","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/safe-lanes/TechnicalMoudle/commits/049305dff1911342a06d4f7fa631463b88acc840"}],"sha":"7d519173051b24a7a0e938ae8723b6ea8f155eb7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/safe-lanes/TechnicalMoudle/commits/7d519173051b24a7a0e938ae8723b6ea8f155eb7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/224569240?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/safe-lanes/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/safe-lanes/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/safe-lanes/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/safe-lanes/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/safe-lanes","id":224569240,"login":"safe-lanes","node_id":"U_kgDODWKnmA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/safe-lanes/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/safe-lanes/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/safe-lanes/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/safe-lanes/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/safe-lanes/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/safe-lanes","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/safe-lanes/TechnicalMoudle/commits/049305dff1911342a06d4f7fa631463b88acc840/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T15:17:59Z","email":"support@sl-sail.com","name":"support"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T15:17:59Z","email":"support@sl-sail.com","name":"support"},"message":"assistant: due-in-period split (calendar vs running hours), lead-time explanation for a running-hours Due, clean-install proof + Windows npm note (pilot-verified, NOT deployed)\n\n1. \"Due this week\": get_due_work_orders now returns calendarDue (calendar-dated jobs within the period)\n   and runningHoursDue (currently Due running-hours jobs) SEPARATELY. Running-hours jobs are never counted\n   in the period figure and never dropped; the result and the model state that their calendar due date\n   cannot be determined from the available hours. Each row carries dueRH, currentRH, rhRemaining,\n   rhLeadTimeHours and rhStatusBasis (\"due hours reached\" | \"N h remaining, within the L h running-hours\n   lead time\"). listWorkOrders rows gain the additive rhLeadTimeHours they were computed with.\n\n2. Wording reconciled: six running-hours jobs are Due - five ME piston inspections at 500 of 500 h, one\n   ME Turbocharger cleaning at 0 of 500 h. The turbocharger is Due because 500 h remaining is within the\n   vessel''s 720 h running-hours lead time (WORK_ORDER_THRESHOLDS.RH_LEAD_TIME_HOURS; the verified rule) -\n   the model says exactly that, never that the hours were reached, and treats the old 0 h reading as\n   needing confirmation on board, not as bad data. PROVEN in the widget (pilot image pilot-r5).\n\n3. Dependency files: a clean `npm ci` from the committed package.json + package-lock.json in a fresh\n   node:22-bookworm-slim container (node v22.23.2, npm 10.9.8) installs 701 packages, remark-gfm 4.0.1\n   resolves and sharp loads with the Linux binaries. The Windows checkout loses its win32 sharp/rollup\n   binaries on every npm install because the lockfile is Linux-generated (no win32 optional packages);\n   repair and rationale documented in docs/DEV-WINDOWS-NPM-OPTIONAL-BINARIES.md.\n\nStill pending, not closable on the emulated single-tenant pilot: genuine SAILERP login; trusted identity\n(client-forwarded headers); multi-tenant Data API authentication gap. tsc 294, tests 58/58.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4ea3f52ec362c4c6bd241610efa49898f68a6c3c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/safe-lanes/TechnicalMoudle/git/trees/4ea3f52ec362c4c6bd241610efa49898f68a6c3c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/safe-lanes/TechnicalMoudle/git/commits/049305dff1911342a06d4f7fa631463b88acc840","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/224569240?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/safe-lanes/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/safe-lanes/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/safe-lanes/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/safe-lanes/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/safe-lanes","id":224569240,"login":"safe-lanes","node_id":"U_kgDODWKnmA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/safe-lanes/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/safe-lanes/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/safe-lanes/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/safe-lanes/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/safe-lanes/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/safe-lanes","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/safe-lanes/TechnicalMoudle/commit/049305dff1911342a06d4f7fa631463b88acc840","node_id":"C_kwDOP13NqNoAKDA0OTMwNWRmZjE5MTEzNDJhMDZkNGY3ZmE2MzE0NjNiODhhY2M4NDA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/safe-lanes/TechnicalMoudle/commit/318df2a8f985de0c9f2f51ea3993ba8a311b5204","sha":"318df2a8f985de0c9f2f51ea3993ba8a311b5204","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/safe-lanes/TechnicalMoudle/commits/318df2a8f985de0c9f2f51ea3993ba8a311b5204"}],"sha":"049305dff1911342a06d4f7fa631463b88acc840","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/safe-lanes/TechnicalMoudle/commits/049305dff1911342a06d4f7fa631463b88acc840"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/224569240?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/safe-lanes/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/safe-lanes/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/safe-lanes/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/safe-lanes/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/safe-lanes","id":224569240,"login":"safe-lanes","node_id":"U_kgDODWKnmA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/safe-lanes/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/safe-lanes/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/safe-lanes/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/safe-lanes/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/safe-lanes/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/safe-lanes","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/safe-lanes/TechnicalMoudle/commits/318df2a8f985de0c9f2f51ea3993ba8a311b5204/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T14:39:53Z","email":"support@sl-sail.com","name":"support"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T14:39:53Z","email":"support@sl-sail.com","name":"support"},"message":"assistant: follow-up context, readable tables, running-hours facts, list paging and how-to starters (pilot-verified, NOT deployed)\n\n1. Follow-ups. The widget always sent conversationHistory; the central service dropped it (PROVEN: ''make that\n   readable'' answered ''what would you like?''). build_history() keeps the last ASSISTANT_HISTORY_MESSAGES (8)\n   messages, each capped at 4000 chars, and passes them as Pydantic AI message_history - through the same\n   masking choke point (G3) as everything else. Tool loop AND documentation path: a short follow-up whose own\n   words retrieve nothing (''explain step 2'') is retried once with the previous user question prepended, and\n   the docs prompt is told that ''step 2'' points at the assistant''s previous answer. Without history (every\n   regression suite) both paths are byte-for-byte the served ones. Rules: data questions always re-call the\n   tool (history is for reformatting only); a changed [App context] vessel never reuses earlier figures; the\n   widget clears the conversation when the selected vessel changes (useChat).\n   Pilot: overdue -> ''make that readable'' -> ''show more'' (rows 11-20) OK; how-to -> ''explain step 2'' OK on the\n   tool loop and on a throwaway docs-only container (live shape); WKFV 142 -> switch to Vessel 4 -> 0 (fresh\n   tool call) OK; widget clears on vessel change (PROVEN in the browser).\n\n2. Tables. react-markdown had no GFM plugin, so pipe tables rendered as raw text. remark-gfm 4.0.1 (pinned) +\n   a horizontally scrolling wrapper for the 400px / phone-width panel. PROVEN: 11-row table rendered inside a\n   314px wrapper. Side effect handled: the install dropped the Windows-only sharp/rollup binaries (reinstalled\n   --no-save; lockfile poison check 0).\n\n3. Running hours. get_due_work_orders / get_overdue_work_orders now return maintenanceBasis, dueRH, currentRH;\n   a date-range filter no longer drops running-hours jobs (PROVEN: ''due this week'' answered 0 while 6 were\n   due). Instructions: quote ''x of y h'', never invent a calendar date, never claim the hours are reached unless\n   currentRH >= dueRH, never invent a reason for Due. Investigated before wording: five ME piston jobs are at\n   500 of 500 h; ME Turbochargers (601.053) is at 0 of 500 h and is Due only because 500 h remaining is within\n   the vessel''s 720 h running-hours lead time (WORK_ORDER_THRESHOLDS.RH_LEAD_TIME_HOURS) - the component''s\n   running hours have been 0.00 since the 19-Feb import (rh_master_update_source=IMPORT). That is PMS data,\n   kept separate from the assistant.\n\n4. Overdue list order. Results carry listOrder (priority first, then days overdue) and oldestOverdue (work\n   order, component, priority, days) so ''256 days'' is attributed (MKR-IN-00044-403.006.01, Low) while the\n   rows shown top out at 254. Paging: offset parameter, 10 rows per call.\n\n5. Starters. Suggested prompts now include four ''How do I ...'' documentation questions (complete a work order,\n   update running hours, create an unplanned work order, add a new spare part) - each verified on the pilot;\n   the model is told to offer how-to options whenever it lists choices.\n\n6. Shore-only enforcement and the vessel-scope rules untouched (re-probed: ship 403, Ship-type user refused).\n   Genuine SAILERP login still PENDING (emulated session only). Tests 58/58, tsc 294.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b8a41bbce289ff7832d27842b1be1f5dbd44f7a6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/safe-lanes/TechnicalMoudle/git/trees/b8a41bbce289ff7832d27842b1be1f5dbd44f7a6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/safe-lanes/TechnicalMoudle/git/commits/318df2a8f985de0c9f2f51ea3993ba8a311b5204","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/224569240?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/safe-lanes/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/safe-lanes/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/safe-lanes/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/safe-lanes/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/safe-lanes","id":224569240,"login":"safe-lanes","node_id":"U_kgDODWKnmA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/safe-lanes/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/safe-lanes/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/safe-lanes/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/safe-lanes/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/safe-lanes/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/safe-lanes","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/safe-lanes/TechnicalMoudle/commit/318df2a8f985de0c9f2f51ea3993ba8a311b5204","node_id":"C_kwDOP13NqNoAKDMxOGRmMmE4Zjk4NWRlMGM5ZjJmNTFlYTM5OTNiYThhMzExYjUyMDQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/safe-lanes/TechnicalMoudle/commit/3bdebf90d2b7e59f7b6233370a13f848b3aa8af4","sha":"3bdebf90d2b7e59f7b6233370a13f848b3aa8af4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/safe-lanes/TechnicalMoudle/commits/3bdebf90d2b7e59f7b6233370a13f848b3aa8af4"}],"sha":"318df2a8f985de0c9f2f51ea3993ba8a311b5204","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/safe-lanes/TechnicalMoudle/commits/318df2a8f985de0c9f2f51ea3993ba8a311b5204"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/224569240?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/safe-lanes/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/safe-lanes/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/safe-lanes/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/safe-lanes/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/safe-lanes","id":224569240,"login":"safe-lanes","node_id":"U_kgDODWKnmA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/safe-lanes/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/safe-lanes/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/safe-lanes/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/safe-lanes/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/safe-lanes/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/safe-lanes","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/safe-lanes/TechnicalMoudle/commits/3bdebf90d2b7e59f7b6233370a13f848b3aa8af4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T13:25:28Z","email":"support@sl-sail.com","name":"support"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T13:25:28Z","email":"support@sl-sail.com","name":"support"},"message":"assistant: shore-only enforcement by deployment mode, screen-matching work-order counts, forwarded user id in the identity token (pilot-verified, NOT deployed)\n\n1. Shore-only. The assistant endpoints (/assistant/manifest|execute|token) are refused with 403 on a\n   ship instance before auth or secrets are looked at, using the application''s existing deployment-mode\n   predicate (syncRole.isShipInstance: SYNC_INSTANCE_ID / sync_settings.instance_id starting ''SHIP-'',\n   DB first) - not role or userType. The widget hides itself on a ship for every role, Sail Admin\n   included, via the existing /sync/instance-info signal (hidden until the mode is known). Verified on\n   both pilot containers: ship (rebuilt from this tree, SHIP-WKFV) 403 x4 incl. a valid shore-minted\n   Sail Admin token + correct secret; shore (SHORE-PILOT) 200; ship Work Orders page renders with no\n   chat button, shore page shows it. Unrelated ship routes unchanged (vessels 200, provision + sync ok).\n   Note: the previous pilot ship image (3-Sep) predated the assistant module (404s), so the ''already\n   enforced'' reading was never true on the same codebase - the routes had no gate (READ).\n\n2. Counts match the Technical screen. Every work-order read in the chatbot tools (15 call sites) goes\n   through getWorkOrdersWithComputedStatus (the CLAUDE.md contract) instead of raw storage rows, and\n   get_work_order_counts reuses computeWorkOrderTabCounts - the exact tab-badge calculation of the Work\n   Orders screen. Pilot vessel, same snapshot: screen tabs Scheduled 1 / Due 6 / Overdue 142 / Pending\n   Approval 4 / Unplanned 1 / Completed 0 / Postponed 0 = assistant. Before: 302 raw rows (149 archived\n   duplicates included) with stale stored statuses (Overdue 140, Active 150).\n\n3. Identity. The minted userId is the forwarded x-user-id for forwarded sessions (was the mock session\n   id ''1'' for every user: one shared rate bucket, useless audit). Trust level unchanged and stated in\n   code: role/userType/userId are client-forwarded SAILERP headers, exactly what the module''s own RBAC\n   guards trust - NOT server-verified. The ''Office = any vessel'' rule is not wider than the module''s\n   existing policy: requireVesselAccess passes every session (mock role) - traced live for Sail Admin,\n   Admin, User, External 1 AND a Ship-type user (all 200 on Vessel 4 from the app API); the assistant\n   refuses the Ship-type user. Tampered token -> 401 bad-signature.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6c1f314d85954a8e771e3fc42c4631812f4a1147","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/safe-lanes/TechnicalMoudle/git/trees/6c1f314d85954a8e771e3fc42c4631812f4a1147"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/safe-lanes/TechnicalMoudle/git/commits/3bdebf90d2b7e59f7b6233370a13f848b3aa8af4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/224569240?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/safe-lanes/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/safe-lanes/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/safe-lanes/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/safe-lanes/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/safe-lanes","id":224569240,"login":"safe-lanes","node_id":"U_kgDODWKnmA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/safe-lanes/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/safe-lanes/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/safe-lanes/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/safe-lanes/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/safe-lanes/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/safe-lanes","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/safe-lanes/TechnicalMoudle/commit/3bdebf90d2b7e59f7b6233370a13f848b3aa8af4","node_id":"C_kwDOP13NqNoAKDNiZGViZjkwZDJiN2U1OWY3YjYyMzMzNzBhMTNmODQ4YjNhYThhZjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/safe-lanes/TechnicalMoudle/commit/8b10ca1967249a083f4fca2e1eda30ef306a032d","sha":"8b10ca1967249a083f4fca2e1eda30ef306a032d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/safe-lanes/TechnicalMoudle/commits/8b10ca1967249a083f4fca2e1eda30ef306a032d"}],"sha":"3bdebf90d2b7e59f7b6233370a13f848b3aa8af4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/safe-lanes/TechnicalMoudle/commits/3bdebf90d2b7e59f7b6233370a13f848b3aa8af4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/224569240?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/safe-lanes/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/safe-lanes/followers","followi